Help Type: topic
Topic: readiness

Readiness

Purpose:
  Use this when `inspect` reports missing `--query` support, generated data, or provider configuration.
  Readiness explains what must exist before `--query`, Reading Graph, summaries, and Knowledge Graph retrieval can work.

Start with inspect:
  {{ commandName }} <archive-uri> inspect

Archive index readiness:
  Ordinary archive source query needs chapter index artifacts. For each content chapter, at least one of these must be current:
  - FTS artifact: `<chapter-uri>/index/fts`
  - Source embedding artifact: `<chapter-uri>/index/embedding/source`

  Summary semantic retrieval is separate:
  - Summary embedding artifact: `<chapter-uri>/index/embedding/summary`
  - Summary embedding alone does not satisfy ordinary archive source query readiness.

  Artifact behavior:
    Chapter artifacts are stored inside the `.wikg` archive.
    Build FTS artifacts locally for an archive or chapter, without provider calls:
      {{ commandName }} wikg://local/job add --input <archive-uri|chapter-uri> --task index-fts
    Build source embedding artifacts with the chapter index URI or queue target `index-embedding-source`.
    Build summary embedding artifacts with the chapter index URI or queue target `index-embedding-summary`.
    Building embedding artifacts requires `wikg://local/config/embeddings` and may call the configured provider.
    Archive input creates one job per eligible chapter. Re-run inspect after the jobs finish to verify query readiness.

  Cache behavior:
    `{{ commandName }} <archive-uri>/index sync` builds or repairs local `index.db` cache from artifacts.
    Sync does not build missing artifacts and does not call an embeddings provider.
    Archive-level query can create a missing cache from current artifacts on first use, but explicit sync avoids the first-query delay.
    If query reports a missing or outdated cache, run `{{ commandName }} <archive-uri>/index sync`; library query always requires a current library cache.
    `{{ commandName }} <archive-uri>/index clean` deletes only the local cache.

  Query behavior:
    FTS artifact only: FTS query.
    Source embedding artifact only: semantic/Dense-only query.
    Both artifacts: Hybrid query with automatic fusion.
    Broad query is grouped by result type first: chapter/title, object, chunk, then source/summary text.
    FTS, Dense, and Hybrid ranking affect ordering inside those result groups and evidence-backed object ranking; they do not flatten the type groups into one global rerank.
    Missing both FTS and source embedding for any content chapter in scope: ordinary query fails.
    Add `--skip-unindexed` to a scope query, `related --query`, or `evidence --query` only when you want to search indexed chapters and ignore uncovered chapters.
    Results produced with `--skip-unindexed` are intentionally partial; inspect coverage before treating absent chapters as negative evidence.
    Summary embedding artifacts are for summary semantic retrieval and are not the minimum requirement for ordinary source query.

  Commands:
    {{ commandName }} <archive-uri>/index
    {{ commandName }} <chapter-uri>/index/fts --help
    {{ commandName }} <chapter-uri>/index/embedding/source --help
    {{ commandName }} <chapter-uri>/index/embedding/summary --help
    {{ commandName }} <archive-uri>/index sync --help
    {{ commandName }} <archive-uri>/index clean --help

Library index readiness:
  Library-wide scopes use an aggregate library index cache built from member archives' artifacts.
  Unlike a free archive, library query does not lazy-sync this cache. It must already be current.

  Default behavior:
    `{{ commandName }} wikg://lib/index sync` rebuilds the default library index cache from registered present archives.
    `{{ commandName }} wikg://lib/<lib-id>/index sync` rebuilds a non-default library index cache.
    The index is local derived state under Wiki Graph staging, not a file inside the library folder.
    Sync does not build missing chapter artifacts and does not call an embeddings provider.

  Stale behavior:
    Library membership changes can make the aggregate index stale.
    Managed archive writes try to sync an existing library index cache immediately.
    Sync the library index when library-wide query reports that it is missing, stale, or not ready.

  Commands:
    {{ commandName }} wikg://lib/index
    {{ commandName }} wikg://lib/index sync --help
    {{ commandName }} wikg://lib/index clean --help
    {{ commandName }} help library

Generation readiness:
  Reading Graph, Reading Summary, and Knowledge Graph data are generated artifacts.
  They do not appear just because source text exists.

  All generation jobs require LLM configuration:
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/llm
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/llm test

  Inspect job commands before starting expensive work:
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/job --help
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/job add --help

LLM readiness:
  `wikg://local/config/llm` is required for generating:
  - Reading Graph
  - Reading Summary
  - Knowledge Graph

  Minimum configuration:
    provider
    model
    provider credentials when required

  Common path:
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/llm put provider openai
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/llm put model gpt-4.1
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/llm put apiKey --secret
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/llm test

Embeddings readiness:
  `wikg://local/config/embeddings` is required for source or summary embedding artifact builds and for querying an index cache that includes Dense vectors.
  Hybrid query can still fall back to FTS if a Dense query embedding request fails.

  Minimum configuration:
    provider
    model
    baseURL when using openai-compatible
    provider credentials when required

  Common path:
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/embeddings put provider openai
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/embeddings put model text-embedding-3-small
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/embeddings put apiKey --secret
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/embeddings test

WikiSpine readiness:
  Knowledge Graph generation also requires WikiSpine.
  WikiSpine provides entity candidate lookup for Knowledge Graph construction.

  Provider choices:
  - `fetch`: use the hosted WikiSpine HTTP service with a WikiGraph API key. This is usually easier for Agents and hosted setups.
  - `cli`: run the local `wikispine` command from PATH. This is useful for offline or locally controlled environments, but requires local runtime setup and data.

  Configure one provider, then test it:
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikispine put provider fetch
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikispine put token --secret
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikispine test

    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikispine put provider cli
    {{ commandName }} wikg://local/config/wikispine test

  Recovery:
    Use `fetch` when network access and an API key for the hosted service are available.
    Use `cli` only when a local `wikispine` executable and its runtime/data are prepared.
    Test `cli` from the same shell that runs Wiki Graph so PATH and runtime files match the job environment.
    CLI help does not install the local WikiSpine runtime; use the guide below when preparing a local setup.
    If the selected provider fails its config test, fix that provider or switch providers before starting Knowledge Graph jobs.

  Runtime setup and recovery guide:
    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oomol-lab/wiki-graph/refs/heads/main/docs/wikispine-runtime.md

How to choose:
  - Need lexical retrieval: build chapter FTS artifacts, then sync cache if you do not want lazy sync.
  - Need semantic retrieval: configure embeddings, build source embedding artifacts, then sync cache.
  - Need both lexical and semantic retrieval: build both FTS and source embedding artifacts, then sync the archive index cache if it already exists or query reports it outdated; query can create a missing archive cache and chooses Hybrid automatically once the cache is current.
  - Need searchable retrieval across a managed folder: sync the library index cache.
  - Need to intentionally drop local cache: clean index cache; artifacts remain in the archive.
  - Need generated Reading Graph or summaries: configure LLM and use local jobs.
  - Need Knowledge Graph: configure LLM and WikiSpine, then use local jobs.
  - Not sure what is missing: run inspect and check index artifact coverage before syncing cache.

